				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Ok... for the past week or so we've had these brainless unemployment rejects coming in from companies who are selling artwork at frame cost. No less than 4 times.
<br />

<br />
Today one comes in and I tell him politely that we are not interested 3 times. After the third time he says "Well of course you're not interested, you haven't even looked." In jumps my office manager, "She told you we're not interested, you don't have to be rude about it, but there IS a no soliciting sign on our front door, now get out."
<br />

<br />
I'm sick of having to deal with these door to door salesmen. I swear I'm going to put a huge sign on the door that reads, "If you're a solicitor DO NOT ENTER THIS STORE! WE'RE NOT INTERESTED!!! YES WE MEAN IT!!!" 
<br />

<br />
Of course some customer would see it and get offended/read it wrong and never come back.</span><span class=sign><br />_________________<br /><img src="http://raveynfyre.home.comcast.net/option1.jpg" border="0" />
